{{NZelectorateShortDesc|current=yes|type=general|region=Southland and Otago}}
'''Southland''' is an electorate to the [[New Zealand House of Representatives]]. It was first created for the [[2020 New Zealand general election]] and has since then been held by [[Joseph Mooney (New Zealand politician)|Joseph Mooney]] of the [[New Zealand National Party|National Party]].

==Population centres==
{{maplink|from=New Zealand Electorates/2020/General/Southland.map|frame=yes|text=Map of boundaries at the [[2020 New Zealand general election|2020]] and [[2023 New Zealand general election|2023]] general elections}}
Despite its name, the electorate straddles the border between the [[Southland, New Zealand|Southland]] and [[Otago]] regions. It is the second-largest general electorate in New Zealand, behind [[West Coast-Tasman]], and is predominantly rural in nature. The electorate includes [[Gore, New Zealand|Gore]], [[Winton, New Zealand|Winton]], [[Mataura]], [[Alexandra, New Zealand|Alexandra]], [[Arrowtown]], [[Queenstown, New Zealand|Queenstown]] and [[Te Anau]] (among others), and much of [[Fiordland National Park]].<ref>{{cite web |url= https://www.vote.nz/map/index.html?id=2&modified=2020110110227 |title=Map of electorates for the 2020 and 2023 electorates |date=17 April 2020 |access-date=18 April 2020}}</ref> In the 2025 boundary review, the electorate's boundary with {{NZ electorate link|Invercargill}} would be moved east of the [[Ōreti River]], transferring away the communities west of [[Winton, New Zealand|Winton]].<ref>{{cite book |title=Report of the Representation Commission 2025 |url=https://elections.nz/assets/pagecomponent-file-files/REPORT-OF-THE-REPRESENTATION-COMMISSION-2025-WEB.pdf |isbn=978-0-473-75233-0 |publisher=Representation Commission |access-date=17 September 2025 |page=21 |date=8 August 2025 }}</ref>

==History==
The Southland electorate emerged at the 2020 redistribution after the [[Clutha District|Clutha]] region moved out of the former electorate of [[Clutha-Southland]]. It comprised the bulk of Clutha-Southland, plus another area around Alexandra that had been moved in from {{NZ electorate link| Waitaki}}. The [[Electoral Commission (New Zealand)|Representation Commission]] initially proposed to move Winton and [[The Catlins]] into {{NZ electorate link| Invercargill}}, but after a public consultation process these areas remained in Southland, which instead shed a large area in West Southland around [[Tuatapere]].<ref>{{cite web|url= https://vote.nz/assets/Boundary-Review/REPORT-OF-THE-REPRESENTATION-COMMISSION-2020.pdf |title= Report of the Representation Commission 2020 |date= 17 April 2020 | access-date= 18 April 2020}}</ref><ref>{{cite news|last= Kelly |first= Rachael |url= https://www.stuff.co.nz/southland-times/southland-top-stories/117563500/changes-to-cluthasouthland-invercargill-electorates-under-proposed-boundary-changes |title= Changes to Clutha-Southland, Invercargill electorates under proposed boundary changes |work= Southland Times |date= 20 November 2019 |access-date= 19 April 2020}}</ref>

The incumbent from the Clutha-Southland electorate, [[Hamish Walker]], announced in July 2020 that he would not contest the Southland electorate.<ref>{{cite news |title=Covid-19 privacy leak: MP Hamish Walker announces he won't stand for re-election |url= https://www.rnz.co.nz/news/political/420754/covid-19-privacy-leak-mp-hamish-walker-announces-he-won-t-stand-for-re-election |accessdate=8 July 2020 |work=[[Radio New Zealand]] |date=8 July 2020|archive-url= https://web.archive.org/web/20200708003402/https://www.rnz.co.nz/news/political/420754/covid-19-privacy-leak-mp-hamish-walker-announces-he-won-t-stand-for-re-election|archive-date=8 July 2020}}</ref> Later that month, the National Party selected [[Joseph Mooney (New Zealand politician)|Joseph Mooney]] as their candidate for this safe National seat.<ref>{{Cite news |last=McKenzie-McLean |first=Jo |url= https://www.stuff.co.nz/national/politics/122317307/queenstown-lawyer-joseph-mooney-selected-to-replace-hamish-walker-as-southland-electorate-candidate |title=Queenstown lawyer Joseph Mooney selected to replace Hamish Walker as Southland electorate candidate |work=[[Stuff (website)|Stuff]] |date=31 July 2020 |access-date=3 August 2020 |archive-url= https://web.archive.org/web/20201023185505/https://www.stuff.co.nz/national/politics/122317307/queenstown-lawyer-joseph-mooney-selected-to-replace-hamish-walker-as-southland-electorate-candidate |archive-date=23 October 2020|url-status=live}}</ref> Mooney was elected by a margin of 5,645 votes over Labour Party candidate Jon Mitchell.<ref name="2020election" />

